From 0e05c86001312adde515b7896c09b20ef4dc1cb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:50:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] (b) v2, part b-3: clsguide: \@kernel@caption@reset in
 one sentence

Round-4 finding R4-L4: clsguide showed, with a code example, how a
package keeps its own \caption and passes only \caption* to the
kernel. That endorses the pattern for one possible user (a hyperref
sketch) who has not asked for it, while the advice of the item is to
keep the kernel \caption. The item now says in one sentence that such
code must start its numbered \caption with \@kernel@caption@reset; why
the settings last that long is documented in ltfloat.dtx.
---
 base/doc/clsguide.tex | 16 ++--------------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/base/doc/clsguide.tex b/base/doc/clsguide.tex
index 3f7f465e0..fe844234d 100644
--- a/base/doc/clsguide.tex
+++ b/base/doc/clsguide.tex
@@ -1580,20 +1580,8 @@ redefine \cs{caption} or \cs{@caption} (see the documentation of
   \verb|\caption*{Text}| gives a numbered caption with the text `*' and a
   list entry, followed by `Text'. It is better to keep the kernel
   definition and to use the hooks and sockets. Code that keeps its own
-  \cs{caption} and passes only \cs{caption*} to the kernel (for example
-  with \verb|\@ifstar{\@kernel@caption*}{...}|) must start its own
-  \cs{caption} with \cs{@kernel@caption@reset}, as the kernel
-  \cs{caption} does: the settings for a \cs{caption*} (described above,
-  and \cs{if@captionstar}) last until the next kernel \cs{caption}, so
-  that a deferred \cs{@caption} still sees them, and this command ends
-  them. For example:
-\begin{verbatim}
-\ifdefined\@kernel@caption
-  \let\my@caption\caption % the package's own \caption
-  \def\caption{\@ifstar{\@kernel@caption*}%
-    {\@kernel@caption@reset\my@caption}}
-\fi
-\end{verbatim}
+  \cs{caption} and passes only \cs{caption*} to the kernel must start its
+  own numbered \cs{caption} with \cs{@kernel@caption@reset}.
 \end{itemize}
 
 
